error[L0520]: the result of `mk` keeps a borrow of a temporary
 --> check/returned_closure_keeps_a_borrow_held_in_an_owned_argument.knv:6:28
  |
1 | (defn mk (names)
  |           ----- the returned closure keeps the borrow that `names` holds
...
6 |   (let (g (mk (vec (as-str (str "a")))))
  |                            ^^^^^^^^^ this temporary is dropped at the end of the statement
  |
  = help: bind the argument with `let` before the statement that binds the result, so it lives as long as the result
